course: dictionary
lesson: 16160
title: Staying strong: the word withstand
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Withstand means to stay strong and not be damaged or broken by something hard, such as heat, cold, wind or weight. You can also use it when you stand firm against an attack or a push. Context helps you here: a bridge must withstand heavy loads, so withstand must mean to hold up under them.
explain: Look at the word parts. With- can mean against, and stand means to stay on your feet. So withstand is like standing against something and not falling over. Try swapping in a simple word: «The bridge must hold up under heavy trucks» makes sense, so withstand is close in meaning to hold up under.
explain: Withstand is a verb, and it changes its form. Today we withstand the wind. Yesterday the tent withstood the storm. Every day the wall is withstanding the waves. Notice that withstood is the past form, so it does not end in -stood with a new spelling.
fact: Withstand means to stay strong and not be damaged by something.
fact: Withstand can also mean to resist an attack or pressure successfully.
fact: Forms of withstand: withstand, withstands, withstood, withstanding.
fact: «The shelter must withstand wind and rain.» In design lessons, we test materials to see what they can withstand.
fact: Useful phrases: withstand the heat, withstand the weight, withstand pressure.
exercise: «The bridge was built to withstand heavy trucks.» What does withstand mean here? | To run away from something | *To stay strong and not break under something | To wash something in cold water | To paint something bright colours
exercise: «The tent could withstand the strong wind all night.» What did the tent do in the wind? | It got louder and louder | It flew away into the sky | It turned into a boat | *It stayed up and was not damaged
exercise: «The castle withstood the enemy's siege for three months.» Find and copy the past form of withstand. | *withstood | siege | castle | months
test: «The pot is made of metal so it can withstand high heat.» Why is the pot made of metal? | So it will be easy to bend | *So it will not be damaged by high heat | So it will make a quiet sound | So it will float on water
test: «She tried to withstand the pressure from the crowd.» What does withstand mean in this sentence? | To shout at the crowd | To agree with the crowd | *To stay strong and not give way to the crowd | To run away from the crowd
exam: Mia says, «The sea wall must withstand the big waves.» What does withstand mean in her sentence? | To play with | To paint over | To hide from | *To stay strong and not be broken by
